The prompt’s negative-number example resolves an important ambiguity: it does not use the sum of absolute-value digits. It treats the leading digit as negative (`-12 ↦ -1 + 2 = 1`), which explains the required `[-1, -11, 1, -12, 11]`. I caught that with the prompt example and am adjusting the helper and invariant to formalize exactly this signed-leading-digit convention.
